body:
### What are you really trying to do?
I'm trying to use [Worker Client Refresh](https://github.com/temporalio/sdk-dotnet/tree/main/src/Temporalio.Extensions.Hosting#worker-client-refresh) to handle the custom authentication required to connect to my self-hosted Temporal cluster. 

### Describe the bug

The example uses a connection string for connecting to Temporal which sort of removes the need for refreshing the client. This doesn't show the likely setup you would end up when needing to use worker client refresh. This, at least for me, caused me to think I could omit the client creation/connection options. In that case you will get an exception thrown indicating that there isn't a client, and configuration to create one. I think a more complete example would help people understand how to setup and use the client updater.

I've added an example in the Minimal Reproduction of a reduced version from my implementation where I need to add custom authentication to the Temporal connection. 

I struggled with whether this should be a bug, a feature request, or something else. It seems to sit in between all categories. This is more to document a more complex example of the worker updater to help people who might be in the same position as me.

### Minimal Reproduction

An example using the worker client updater for a custom client creation scenario.

``` csharp
using System;
using System.Threading;

public delegate ITemporalClient CreateAuthenticatedClient(string token);

static class ServiceExtensions
{
  public static void AddTemporal(this IServiceCollection serviceCollection)
  {
    // This provides a way for on-going client updates after the initial client expires
    serviceCollection.AddSingleton<TemporalWorkerClientUpdater>();

    // Custom implemented class to retrieve a client for uses other than the Temporal Worker
    // It is also used by the TemporalAuthUpdaterService to create new clients when the auth changes
    serviceCollection.AddSingleton<TemporalClientProvider>();

    // This provides the initial client used by AddHostedTemporalWorker
    // This is required as the hosted temporal worker requires either a client, or client connect options,
    // or a connection string at startup. It doesn't matter whether the client will be immediately replaced by
    // an updated from the worker client updater
    serviceCollection.AddTransient<ITemporalClient>(services =>
    {
      var conn = services.GetRequiredService<AuthenticatedTemporalConnection>();
      var options = services.GetRequiredService<IOptions<TemporalClientOptions>>().Value;
      return new TemporalClient(conn, options);
    });

    // This wraps the interaction with IServiceProvider to create a new connection/client instead of directly adding it
    // to the TemporalClientProvider
    serviceCollection.AddSingleton<CreateAuthenticatedClient>(services =>
      token =>
      {
        var connection = ActivatorUtilities.CreateInstance<AuthenticatedTemporalConnection>(services, token);
        var options = services.GetRequiredService<IOptions<TemporalClientOptions>>().Value;
        return new TemporalClient(connection, options);
      }
    );

    // Background service to trigger periodic updates
    serviceCollection.AddHostedService<TemporalAuthUpdaterService>();

    serviceCollection.AddHostedTemporalWorker("dealer-connect-jobs")
      // Add activities
      .ConfigureOptions()
      .Configure<TemporalWorkerClientUpdater>((options, updater) => options.WorkerClientUpdater = updater);
  }
}

public class TemporalAuthUpdaterService(TemporalClientProvider provider) : BackgroundService
{
  protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)
  {
    while (!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested)
    {
      // Periodically update check and update the client
      await provider.UpdateClient(stoppingToken);
      await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromHours(1), stoppingToken);
    }
  }
}

public class TemporalClientProvider(CreateAuthenticatedClient creator, TemporalWorkerClientUpdater updater)
{
  public async Task UpdateClient(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
  {
    if (IsClientChangeRequired())
    {
      var client = await creator("token");
      updater.UpdateClient(client);
    }
  }

  private bool IsClientChangeRequired()
  {
    // Determine whether we need to replace the client
    return false;
  }
}
```

### Environment/Versions

<!-- Please complete the following information where relevant. -->

- OS and processor: Mac/Linux
- Temporal SDK Version: 1.9.0
- Self-hosted on Azure using Auth0 for application/connection authentication
